sourceDefinition(class) -> source record or error
  Require a class discovered by the source browser. Read its selected definition,
  resolve filesystem paths and digest the source. Mark embedded/foreign definitions
  read-only in the native editor.

validateSourceDefinition(class, file, source)
  Parse exactly one class in the file's native syntax. Require the same name.
  Resolve superclass declarations and reject unavailable parents and cycles.

sourceStore.save(file, expected digest, source)
  Serialize writes, reread and compare the digest, preserve permissions, write/sync
  a sibling temporary file, then atomically replace. Clean up the temporary file.

sourceGit(file, selector, arguments) -> typed result and Git object ID
  Create/reuse a rooted ordinary Git object for the source directory.
  Send directory configuration and the requested Git method with typed arguments.

POST /source(action, class, source, digest, revision, message) -> SourceResponse
  read: current definition and latest thirty Git file revisions.
  save: validate and compare/write; return updated source/digest and history.
  revision: validate full hexadecimal revision, read historical file via Git.
  diff: return the selected file's working diff from Git.
  commit: require message and current digest; stage/commit only this file via Git.
  Preserve source success independently of unavailable Git metadata.

Saving changes subsequent class loads. Existing object processes retain loaded code.
